Germany: the fourth vaccination against coronavirus is unavoidable
Quarter vacillations will be required in the summer or autumn of 2022.
According to the expert, the current vaccination in Germany will not become the final, but will continue with a new force.
“Despite an active vaccinating campaign in Germany, neither two nor three doses of the coronavirus vaccine will probably not be enough to complete protection.
Ulrich Vageldt, the head of the Association of General Practitioners Ulrich Weigladt is convinced of this.
About it on Saturday, December 11, reports Die Welt.
“We expect that the fourth vaccination will be required in the summer, at the latest in the autumn”, – said the expert.
In addition, Weigeldt hopes that the fourth vaccination against the coronavirus can be carried out “in combination with vaccination against the flu”.
This will help to achieve the best of the best results.
In addition, increased vaccination can help in the fight against the spread of a new strain of coronavirus "Omicron".
And the new option is especially dangerous.
So, the probability of re-infection "Omicron" is three times higher than the strands of Delta or Beta.
this is evidenced by the results of a preliminary study carried out in South Africa.
Proceeding from this, BioNTech / Pfizer manufacturers by March of 2022 are planned to provide a vaccine adapted to Omikron.
The companies emphasize that the two doses of the vaccine do not provide sufficient protection against infection with a new variant of the coronavirus “Omicron”.
A BioNTech and Pfizer study showed that at two doses of the vaccinate, efficacy is significantly lower: “neutralizing potential is reduced by more than 25 times.”
“This points to the fact that the two doses of BNT162b2 do not provide sufficient protection against omicron-staff infection,” said BioNTech and Pfizer.
Therefore, a third dose is required.
Experts insist on accelerating the rate of vaccination in the country.
For example, the Chairman of the German Infectious Disease Society Burd Salzberger advocates a reduction in the interval between the second and the third vaccination.
Moreover, according to Salzberger, expedited vaccination will have an influencing the spread of both the delta-virus and the omicron variant of the coronavirus.
“The experience of Israel very complicates this very convincingly”, – said the expert.
