In Libya said about 7 thousand Russian mercenary mercenaries
In Libya there are more than 7 thousand mercenaries of a private military company (PMC) Wagner.
This was stated on Sunday, December 12, the Chairman of the Supreme state Council Khaled al-Mishri.
“At the moment in Libya there are more than 7 thousand mercenaries mercenaries Wagner PMC.
They also have planes.
They also dig trenches in Sirte and Koufra.
They have 30 reactive aircraft at Gardabiya air bases (also used as a civilian airport in Sirte)”, – quotes his words the agency Anadolu.
Khaled al-Mishri also pointed out that Russian mercenaries “try to seize” the central part of Libya, stretching from Chad to the Mediterranean sea, after “bringing their man to power” in the Central African Republic.
Sacrifice Presence
According to the interlocutor of the publication, Moscow was looking for the country to maintain its presence in North Africa and “separated in Libya”.
“Wagner” is located in Libya since 2019, uses the air base and a port in Sirte, as well as an air base in Jufre, according to the agency’s publication.
The Russian authorities officially denies that Wagner PMCs enjoy the support of the Kremlin.
Where Else mercenaries Can Be
According to the agency, Wagner allegedly operates in nine countries in Africa - the CAR, Libya, the Sudan, Mozambique, the Guinea, Guinea-Bissau, Madagascar, Zimbabwe and Angolese.
The company ensures military training of local forces, the personal protection of the leaders and the protection of energy facilities.
In exchange for these services subsidiaries "Wagner" obtain certain privileges and licenses for the use of minerals and natural resources, as well as for the supply of weapons, technology and military services to these countries.
According to media reports, “Wagnerites” allegedly fought in the Donbass, Syria, Mozambique, Sudan and the CAR.
This group is not listed either in law enforcement agencies or in the register of legal entities, and its fighters are not present in the form list of personnel.
This company is under U.S. Sanctice.
We will remind, earlier the permanent representative of 27 countries of the EU approved restrictions against “Wagner”.
It is expected that this decision of the Council of the European Union will be approved on December 13.
The situation in Libya
The Supreme state Council of Libya is de facto the second chamber of parliament with consultative functions with dominant Islamists, writes TASS.
This body has repeatedly called for the rescheduling of a single voting day on the elections of deputies of the parliament and the head of state from December 24 at least to February 2022.
“There are less than two weeks left before the elections, and the chances that they will pass on time are rapidly declining,” the statement said.
Against this backdrop, the Higher Electoral Commission of Libya has postponed for an indefinite period announcing the final list of nominees, Sky News Arabia reports.
