The government of Dubai has completely renounced a piece of paper - all public services also became only digital
The government of Dubai announced the complete abandonment of paper-film and the transition to digital technologies.
All state services to the population will also be provided exclusively in electronic form.
This is reported by the emirate news agency WAM.
“Today marked the beginning of a new stage of digitalization of all aspects of the life of Dubai – we have completed the transition to a completely reckless government”, – said on Saturday the hered-innovation prince of the emirate, Chairman of the Executive Council of Dubai, Sheikh Hamdan bin Mohammed bin Rashid Al Maktoum.
Now the internal and external virtual circulation in all public institutions of Dubai will be carried out only in digital form through special information platforms.
The innovation touched all industries without exception: health, utilities, the police, municipal bodies, the courts, etc. Many commercial structures also joined the government’s initiative.
The transition to an e-governing government and the digitalization of document circulation began in Dubai in 2018.
During this time, according to the authorities, saved 336 million paper sheets, amounting to 14 million hours of human labor and $ 353.8 million in monetary terms.
Earlier, Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin said that electronic services save citizens 2 days a year.
