The production and export of Turkish cars has fallen below the level of 2020
The production and export of Turkish cars fell sharply in November amid depreciating lira depreciation.
As a result, the indicators of the industry for 11 months turned out to be worse than last last year's result, Bloomberg reports, referring to data from the Association of Automobile Manufacturers of Turkey.
According to the association, 115 thousand cars were produced from factories in Turkey, which is 20% less than a year earlier.
About 75.9 thousand cars were exported for export, which is more than 25% inferior to last year's figure.
And and if according to the results of the first 10 months of this year the automotive sector of Turkey showed a positive dynamic for last year, according to the last 11 months of 2021, the production of cars turned out to be already 0.3% worse than last year's figure.
The reason for such a fall was the sharp weakening of the Turkish lira, which in November fell by 29% compared to the dollar.
This led to a decline in economic activity in all industries.
more than 500 SME entities received a deferral of credit payments in 2021
First Deputy Prime Minister Alikhan Smailov spoke about the situation to provide benefits for small and medium-sized businesses, Kazinform correspondent reports.
“According to the information of the Agency for the regulation and development of the financial market, this year, in accordance with the instructions of the head of state dated April 1, 2021, an order dated April 1, 2021 was adopted by the Chairman of the Agency dated April 9, 2021 “On approving the Procedure for Providing Deferred Payments on Loans of Small and Medium-Sized Businesses,” Alikhan Smailov wrote in his response to a deputy’s request.
He reminded that the procedure for granting deferral of payments on loans provided for the provision by banks and organizations carrying out microfinancial activities for deferred payments on loans issued before April 1, 2021 to SME entities, in the period from April 1 to June 30, 2021.
The deferral period ranged from 30 to 90 days at the choice of an SME subject.
In the application of the borrower could indicate a different period of deferral of payments.
In the period of deferment in respect of the borrower, the claim and claim work were suspended, a notification on the need to repay an overdue registrance, as well as the collection by the creditor of commissions and other payments”, – said the Deputy Prime Minister.
For the year in the second-tier banks received applications for the deferral of payments on loans of 603 borrowers-secrets of SME, of which 553 SME entities in the amount of 9.7 bilbilgions received a deferment.
MFIs submitted applications for a deferral of 131 SME subjects, of which the postponement was provided to 95 entities in the amount of 105.8 million tenge, ”conciled A. Smailov.
