Immunologists hypothesized why obese people become victims of covid
The authors of the work studied the adipose tissue left of bariatric operations, and found that fat cells, known as adipocytes, can be infected with the coronavirus.
Immune cells, located in adipose tissue, macrophages, also became infected, while showing a strong inflammatory reaction.
The scientists also examined the adhesive clairvoyance of patients who died from covid and found coronavirus particles in the fat that surrounded various organs.
It is known that viruses of HIV and influenza can hid in adhesilant tissue, using it as a reservoir in an effort to avoid an immune system.
It’s likely that SARS-CoV-2 is capable.
Biologist told about the causes of dement
Candidate of biological Sciences Semyon Golosheikin called the reasons for the appearance of dementia and spoke about the methods of its prevention in an interview with Sputnik radio.
More than 55 million
Syndrome is manifested by a gradual loss of cognitive functions - over time, a person has difficulty orients even in a familiar environment.
Golosheykin noted that neurodegenerative disturbances, head injuries, certain infections, metabolic disturbances and a lack of certain vitamins often lead to dement.
Some factors increase the risk of developing the disease.
This includes hypertension, diabetic, increased cholesterol, obesity, depression and alcoholism.
At the behavioral level, such factors such as social incommunication and the absence of active cognitive activity is possible,” he said.
The development of dementia is also also influenced by adjudicial habits - smoking, alcohol abuse, sleep disturbances and a part-time lifestyle.
Among the first specimens, the expert noted forgetfulness, the inability to concentrate and a decrease in the level of abstract thinking.
“There is a discussion that hearing loss can be both an early manifestation of Alzheimer’s disease, and one of the risk factors for its occurrence,” the biologist added.
To prevent the occurrence of the disease, WHO recommends to maintain the necessary level of physical exertion, to train cognitive skills and abilities that require the involvement of memory and logic.
