The immunologist said revaccination after 4-5 months will help to protect against the strain of coronavirus “omicron”
Revaccination after four to five months can protect against a new strain of coronavirus coronavirus "omicron".
Such a statement was made by immunologist Nikolay Kryuchkov, who called the vaccination in six months, taking into account the emergence of a new strain, a “very great period”
“With the previous strains, such a period was normal, but now it is best to carry out the procedure in five months, and for people with chronic diseases – in four,” the expert said, urging in parallel with a vaccination campaign to engage in revaccination.
Kryuchkov also noted that early revaccination provides a good titer of neutralizing antibodies.
“If a person was given two vaccinations and a buster, either he was ill and vaccinated or vaccinated and became ill, then he received “hybrid immunity”, that there are a lot of antibosses and neutralizing is enough,” the expert said.
“Big seven” warned Russia about “large-scale consequences”, in the event of an invasion of Ukraine
The G7 (Great G7, Germany, Italy, Canada, the United States, France and Japan) published a statement following the meeting of foreign foreign ministers in Liverpool.
It emphasizes that “military aggression” of Russia against Ukraine “will have huge consequences and it will do dearly” to Moscow, but specific measures are not described in the document.
“We, the foreign Ministers of Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan, the United Kingdom and the United States of the United States of America and the High Representative of the European Union, are united in our condemnation of Russia’s increased military strength and aggressive rhetoric against Ukraine,” the statement said.
Next, the ministers urge Russia to “weak the escalation, use of diplomatic channels and comply with their international obligations with regard to the transparency of military activities,” which U.S. President Biden said during a video call to Russian President Putin on December 7.
“We are reaffirming our support for the efforts of France and Germany in the Normandy format to achieve full implementation of the Minsk agreements in order to resolve the conflict in the East of Ukraine”, – said the foreign ministers of the “Big seven”.
Any use of force to change borders is severely prohibited by international law.
“Russia shouldn’t be in doubt that further miliary aggression against Ukraine will have huge consequences and a serious price in response.”
We reaffirm our unwavering adherence to the sovereignty and territorial violators of Ukraine, as well as the right of any sovereign state to determine their future.
We appreciate the restrained Possible Possible Position
We will intensify our co-operation on our common and comprehensive response," he said in a statement.
Earlier in the first day, the head of British diplomacy Elizabeth Truss said that Russia will be “serious consequences” in the event of an intrusion into Ukraine.
According to her, this meeting showed “a single voice of the G7 countries that account for 50% of the world’s world’s GDP, which made it very clear that the invatization of Ukraine will have huge consequences for Russia.”
Pfizer Vaccine Is Considered 32 Times Less Efficient From Omicron Strain
Pfizer-BioNTech vaccine against the omicron stratum of the coronavirus is 32 times lower compared to the rest of the disease.
To this conclusion was made by scientists from the University of Hong Kong and the Chinese University of Hong Kong, reports the South China Morning Post (SCMP).
Vaccine was considered less effective on the basis of a study of anti-varial activity in citizens who have received two doses of COVID-19.
“We can see that the majority of people had a high level of antiviral activity against the original Sars-CoV-2 variant, but this ability was significantly reduced against omicron variety”, – Said Professor Malik Peyris.
At the same time, scientists stressed that vaccination remains the most reliable way to protect against the severe course of the disease when infected with the coronavirus.
Earlier, scientists of the London Hygiene and Tropical Medicine school predicted the development of a coronavirus pandemic, taking into account the impact of an omicron strain.
The authors of the study came to the conclusion that the omicron strain can cause a new wage of circulation of the virus and an increase in mortality, if you do not take additional measures.
The head of the Ministry of defense of Ukraine accused Germany of blocking the supply of NATO weapons to Kiev
The head of the Ministry of defense of Ukraine Oleksiy Reznnikov accused the government of former German Chancellor Angela Merkel of blocking Kiev’s acquisition of deadly weapons within NATO.
In an interview with the Financial Times on December 12 Reznikov recalled that last month Germany veto the purchase of anti-sniper systems and rifles to destroy drones.
At the same time it is noted that later Berlin softened its position regarding the rifles, declaring their non-left weapons.
According to the Minister of defense, Kiev intends to seek the acquisition of the above-mentioned weapons within the framework of bilateral agreements with its allies.
In particular, we are talking about the United States, Great Britain, Lithuania and France.
In the meantime, FT notes that the position of the new German government led by Chancellor Olaf Scholz regarding the resolution of arms supplies to Ukraine remains unclear.
Earlier on Sunday, the Ambassador of Ukraine to Germany Andriy Melnyk expressed the opinion that Kiev should not be waiting for the supply of weapons from Berlin under Chancellor Scholz.
According to him, the previous leadership of the Federal Republic of Germany explained its refusal to provide weapons at the risk of developing a military escalation of the conflict in the Donbass, despite the “occulation by Russia” of part of the Ukrainian territory.
Such an “misphilet” stance, the diplomat I am sure, Germany will retain under the new chancellor.
In August, the Ukrainian leader Volodymyr Zelensky said that Kiev is awaiting assistance from Berlin in equipping the navy.
In Ukraine they expect that Germany “will be a partner of Ukraine in a technical sense”, the president added.
It was also noted that in the spring of this year, the co-chairman of the “Green” party of Germany Robert Habek visited the republic, where he spoke in favor of selling defensive weapons to Kiev.
