In Moscow named the winners of the award named after Arseniyev - Rossiyskaya Gazeta
Celebratory ceremony of awarding the winners of the third season of the All-Russian Literary Award "Dornay Vostok".
V. K. Arseniyeva was held in Moscow.
As it is reported on the page of the award in Instagram, a total of 89 applications have been submitted to the organizing committee this season.
Selection passed 63.
The leaders in the number of submitted works were Primorsky and Khabarovsk territories - 13 and 11 applications.
More than 60 works were put forward in three categories: "Long prose", "Short prose", "Sprobe for children".
Nine works - three in each nomination.
The winner in the "Long prose nomination" was Alexander Filkin (Primorsky Krai) with the book "Inscribish on the Glasm".
The award was presented to the vioperator by the Deputy Prime Minister-pendiliated representative of the President of the Russian Federation in the Far Eastern Federal Investigator Yuri Trutnev.
In the nomination "Short prose" the best recognized Lyube Bezbakh (Sakhalin region) with the work "Which of Night Rain whistle".
She received the award from the Minister of the Russian Federation for the Development of the Far East and the Arctic Alexei Chekunkov.
In the nomination “Children prose” the laureate was Trans-Baikal writer Nina Belomestnova and her “Grolord Thread”.
The author was awarded the screenwriter, writer, candidate of philological sciences and the chairman of the Jury Andrey Gelasimov.
All the winners will receive 500 thousand rubles.
We will remind, as part of the "Daalient Vostok" the authors of the best works on the Far Eastern themes are awarded.
The main task of the award is not only to reward the winners and to talk about modern authors, but also to attract cultural interest in the Far East, as a territory for the priority development of the 21st century.
Novels, stories, collections of novels or stories, as well as documentary prose and memoirs can be put forward to the application.
At the same time, it does not matter the author's place of residence, the main thing is to write in Russian.
The official website of the award: https://Premiyaarseyeva.rf/.
