“Mercedes” filed a protest against the result of the Grand Prix of Abu Dhabi
The German team “Mercedes”, whose pilot Lewis Hamilton at the Grand Prix Abu Dhabi finished the second after the Red Bull racer Max Verstappen, filed a protest for the final result of the race, according to the press service of “Formula 1”.
“Mercedes” believes that during the race were violated the rules of “Formula 1” 48.12 and 48.8.
In the first case, the German team disputes the decision of the referees to return circular riders into the same glimpse with the leaders.
According to the latter - Verstappen was ahead of Hamilton to the permitted "restart" zone.
We will add that now the result of the Abu Dhabi Grand Prix, according to which Verstappen ahead of Hamilton by 2,256 seconds and won the world championship “Formula 1” are preliminary, when “Mercedes” protests will be considered notorious
The G7 has warned Russia about the responsibility for the invasion of the invasion of Ukraine
The foreign ministers of the G7 countries warned of “serious consequences” for Russia, if it continues its military aggression against Ukraine, stated in the final statement of the parties.
The participants of the meeting also noted that they condemn the intensification of the Russian armed of these at the country's borders.
“Russia should have no doubt that further military aggression against Ukraine will have serious consequences and serious costs”, – said in a statement published on the website of the British government.
The G7 ministers and the EU’s High Representative noted “unity in their condemnation of Russian armed reinforcement and aggressive rhetoric against Ukraine”.
The British foreign Minister Elisabery Trus at a press conference in Liverpool warned of “big consequences” for Russia in the event of an invasion of Ukraine.
We have made it clear that any intrusion will have significant consequences.
The G7 wants Russia to renounce its aggression against Ukraine,” she said (quoted according to TASS).
Earlier at the summit in Liverpool, the G7 foreign ministers agreed that in order to resolve the crisis due to the build-up of Russian troops on the border with Ukraine, the parties need to return to the negotiating table.
We are talking about negotiations in the “Normandy format”.
The North Atlantic Alliance also advocated a dialogue on Ukraine in the “Normandy format”.
The representative of the Russian foreign Ministry Maria Zakharova said that, urging Russia and Ukraine to return to the negotiating table, the G7 countries “painted in the inability to take responsibility for their own mistakes”.
