The Ministry wants to give the writers the residences
The state will donate federal property retained inherited from the Union of Writers of the USSR and the Literary Fund of the U.S.R."
On its basis will be created writer's residencies will be created, the "Parliamentary Newspaper" was told in the Ministry, which will become the founder of the fund.
The Ministry is preparing a draft presidential decree on the establishment of the Fund for Support of Russian Writers.
The explanatory note stipulates that the fund will be instructed, among other things, about the targeted use and preservation of buildings and buildings, which once belonged to the Soviet Union of Writers and Litfond.
A significant number of immovable property objects previously belonged to the Literary Fund of the U.S.S.R., Including objects located in the town of Writers of Peredelkino, Komarovo village of the Leningrad region and others," the press service of the Ministry of Finance said in a "Parliamentary Newspaper".
The draft decree prescribes to be reflected in the charter of the Fund that it is “created in order to promote literary activity by creating the necessary conditions for the creative work of writers”.
“Creating “creating conditions for creative activity” means the creation on the basis of the transferred property in different regions of Russia of a writer’s residency, in which there would be comfortable conditions for creativity”, – explained in the Ministry of Digital Affairs to our publication.
