Physicians warned about the danger of prolonged use of blood-threat drugs after COVID-19 and before vaccinating
Physicians Irina Yartseva and Sergey Tokarev warned about the danger of uncontrollable use of clutter-threats after a coronavirus COVID-19 infection and before being vaccinated against the coronavirus.
Therapeutic, immunologist Irina Yartseva said that self-prophylaximation of the possible formation of thrombus after COVID-19 can provoke a stroke.
Yartseva explained that blood-thieving preparations are not intended for everyone, only if the patient was hospitalized, was in the hospital, he was diagnosed with complications.
The doctor prescribes anticoagulants (creasing drugs, prevent the excessive formation of throtts) according to indications.
She said that now there is obscurantism - everyone in a row drink anticoagulants for a long time and receive complications in the form of hemorrhagic stroke on this background (brain hemorrhage).
The chief prophylactologist of the Ural Federal District, the scientific director of the Society of Preventive Medical Specialists, MD Sergey Tokarev in an interview with URA.RU said that indistinguishably anticoagulants Russians now often use before vaccination against a coronavirus infection before being vaccinated against coronavirus infection.
According to doctor Tokarev, citizens believe dubious tips on the Internet and begin to self-medicate.
There are such citizens who a week before vaccination by their own decision begins to take anticoagulants.
And when pre-examinated before being vaccinated, doctors notice bruising.
He stressed that it is extremely dangerous to take any medicine without fictitifying the cause of any symptom.
