In China recorded a new case of human infection with avian influenza virus
A new case of human infection with high-pathogenic H5N6 avian influence has been recorded in China.
This was reported by the radio station RTHK with reference to the notétution of health agencies of Hong Kong, reports TASS.
Infection infected a 68-year-old inhabitant of Huyzhou city district in the southern province of Guangdong, who kept a poultry in the farm.
His condition is evaluated by doctors as critical.
The world's first human infection with the H5N6 virus strain was recorded in May 2014 in the southwestern province of Sichuan.
Since then, the number of such cases in the country has reached 53.
