The WHO has discovered “omicron” already in six dozen states
The World Health Organization (WHO) said that a new strain of coronavirus "omicron" has already been identified in 63 countries.
A number of experts have already said that the spread of a new strain can have disastrous consequences.
About the pace of distribution of the strain said in a WHO report.
According to the organization, as of December 9, the strain has already been detected in 63 countries, in all six regions of the WHO.
Despite the fact that he began to actively spread only from the end of November.
The WHO is also concerned about the rapid propagation of the new variant of the coronavirus.
WHO experts express concern that the new strain according to preliminary data can bypass the prevalence of the “delta strain”, aka the Indian variant of the coronavirus, which is now the leader in all absolutely countries without exception.
Prior to this, the Director-general of the World Health Organization, Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus, said that the omicron strain can have a significant effect on the course of the coronavirus pandemic.
Similar conclusions have also been reached in the U.G.
Experts of the London Hygiene and Tropical Medicine (LSHTM), believe that “omicron” in the coming months will supplant the “delta”.
And the number of cases only in the United Kingdom will amount to about 1 million. This despite the fact that officially "omicron" at the present moment a few hundred people get sick in the Kingdom, and according to estimated data up to 10 thousand.
British experts predict tens of thousands of deaths from Omicron strain, and more than 2 thousand people will be taken to hospitals every day.
what the British health care system will not be able to cope with will not be able to cope with.
