Hackers have hacked the Twitter of the Prime Minister of India
Hackers have hacked the Twitter account of Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi.
Involuntescrenants managed to publish a fake message.
It is reported that India allegedly recognized bitcoin as a legal means of payment, as well as that the country has already purchased a cryptocurrency.
Modi’s office was asked to ignite new messages.
The representatives of the Prime Minister said that on Twitter quickly responsibly - access to the account was restored.
The Indian prime minister’s page has already been hacked in 2020 and called for donatings to the fund using cryptocurrency.
Referendum in New Caledonia Votes Against Independence in New Caledonia
In New Caledonia, the third referendum, held on 12 December, ended with the same result as the previous two.
According to the first partial results pronounced at noon on Sunday, December 12, the majority of New Caledonia residents voted during a referendum against the independence of their territory.
At the same time, the level of participation in this third vote was significantly lower than in the previous two.
According to the preliminary results published published by the local authorities, 3.51% (2 755 people who voted, while 96,49% (75,762) (75,762) voted.
The appearance was 43.90%, more than 80 thousand residents of New Caledonia took part in the elections.
According to these interim results, France-Presse said, “the outcome of these elections did not leave a place for doubt”, as supporters of independence urged voters not to participate in the vote.
Being initiators of the referendum, they spoke out against its holding on December 12, believing that a new COVID-19 epidemic outbreak in the archipelago interferes with a full-fledged and “honest” election campaign.
Thus, this inparticipation paved the way to the third victory of supporters of French New Caledonia, after the referendums held in November 2018 and in October 2020.
in 2018, 56.7% of the population voted against independence, in 2020 - 53.3%.
As stated by the separatists, they do not recognize the results of the last vote and will dissuade them in the United Nations.
As reported on Sunday, December 12, in the Elysee Palace, French President Emmanuel Macron should speak on the results of this referendum.
New Caledony’s independence has largely revitalized the last weeks of the presidential campaign in France.
Several presidential candidates spoke in favor that the territory remained part of France, since it is “the last region of the presence of the European Union in the Pacific”.
“The New Caledonia must remain French,” Eric Zemmour said many times.
The same statement was made by Republican candidate Valerie Pecress, which at the end of October published a column in Le Figaro, urging Caledonians to remain French.
For its part, Emmanuel Macron announced in May 2018 that he will not take a position, "because it is not his responsibility."
Nevertheless, the President added: “France would be less preserved without New Caledonia.”
Prime Minister Jean Casteks, for his other part, expressed “a strong desire that the choice of Caledonians should be the choice of France”.
