Ukraine will begin to produce retigulators of a new generation
In the new Ukrainian-Turkish plant will begin to create retactive unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) type ANKKA.
On December 11, this was reported by a freelvant adviser to the head of the office of the Ukrainian President Oleksiy Arestovich.
That is, they are able to act against airborne objects, against other drones.
Even against mandable aviation.
They will have Ukrainian engines and other Turkish avionics: the hull and so on,” Dialog.ua quotes him as saying.
commenting on the main features of ANKA devices, Arestovich said that we are talking about repulsive, not piston UAVs.
According to him, this is a new generation of drones after Bayraktar, which exceed it "in all characteristics."
The first batch of the UAV should be produced by the plant at the end of next year, Arestovich concluded.
ANKA aircraft was established by the Turkish Aerospace Agency in February 2014.
The development of the drone was conducted by the Turkish authorities in cooperation with a number of private companies since 2010.
On the eve of the Ukrainian General headquarters classified data on the use of Bayraktar drones and Javelin missile complexes during military operations of the combined forces in the Donbas.
December 6, the President of Ukraine Volodymyr Zelensky said that in the country began the construction of a plant for the manufacture of modern military drones.
According to him, Ukraine intends to use drones.
On September 29, Bayraktar Savunma and the Ukrainian Ministry of Defense signed an agreement on the construction in the Kiev region of the center, which will conduct personnel training, as well as the testing and maintenance of Turkish Bayraktar UAV.
