Demand for superyachts has risen in the world by a quarter
The construction of super-yakhtes this year and orders for the next year are beating all records in the world, despite calls to reduce the hydrocarbon footprint and the fight against climatic changes.
In the world register of vessels, the number of ordered yachts amounted to 1200 units - a quarter more than last year.
In an era to combat the consequences of climate change for reducing greenhouse gas emissions, it is difficult to imagine that the number of people, who have the desire and money per floating fortress for $ 50 million or higher, will not decrease, writes “Gardian”.
However, they are becoming more and more of them.
This year was ordered 25% more vessels than in the previous year.
Brokers say there hasn’t been such excitement in the market for 20 years.
The main reason is that many who can afford the yacht are afraid of contamination on land and prefer to hide from the pandemic aboard its own vessel.
The second reason is also associated with the coronavirus.
If before all these people went to the office and met with business partners in person, now the vast majority of them are working remotely, and negotiations are carried out in zoom.
Broker Will Christie told the newspaper that the shipyards take orders for new yachts for 2025 and later.
This means that the customers are ready to pay more, as long as their Yacht was ready at least for a year or twice earlier.
“People just thirst for freedom and the super-wealth could afford it,” he says.
In Western society, many criticize such behavior of the rich and call it decadent.
Welwomen, sociologists do not want to understand that in the days of spending traveling to space, living on yachts or flying their own planes cause irritation in society, since the elite does not want to share responsibility for climate change with the rest of humanity.
Economists call on governments to take action and are proposing to introduce new taxes and rules for super-wealth, although they understand that with such mobility of money, it will be extremely difficult to achieve this.
In the meantime, only the number of super-yyachts is imminent, but also their characteristics.
Of 1,200 1,27 have stern length above 100 meter.
The Norwegian billionaire Rekke builds a 183-meg Tremble yacht REV Ocean with a length.
After the launch, it will be the largest yacht in the world.
On the yacht there is an "moon swimming pool", as well as a submarine designed to study the depth of porridge.
On the existing super-yachts, sites for helicopters, open-air theaters have become ordinary, and in some of them, as, for example, on the yacht wander McGregor - a platform for martial fracturing became.Professional economic anthropology of the American anthropology of the American University in Indiana Richard Wilk says that compared with the total number of greenhouse gases, a carbone trace produced by the super-wealth is insensible.
But it has a symbolic meaning, given that multi-billionaires in the world a little more than 2000 people.
This is just another example of overconsumpsation of a very small group of people.
Scientists have found that the emissive trace of billionaires is a thousand times the trace of the average inhabitant of the planet.
If one person produces an average of 5 tons of CO2 per annum per anniversaries, the largest polltanger of the planet Roman Abramovich is responsible for 33.9 tons of greenhouse gases that entered the atmosphere in 2018.
At the same time, two-thirds of the emissive footprint sanctuated on his yacht Eclipse with a length of 162.5 meter.
Even if there is no owner on board the yacht, the team continues to poison the planet.
The Owner can call the captain and give the command to drive the yacht, for example, from the Mediterranean to the Caribbean.
Owners of superyachts do not speculate among other people when they, as Australia's richest woman, Jina Reinhard, who owns mines on the continent, are complaining through the Youtube that for their gig giant ships there is no place for a berjudicial.
