Determined a dangerous week's dose of alcohol, leading to the development of intestinal intestinal cancer
American scientists have determined what volume of alcoholic beverages in a week increases the risk of developing cancer.
About it writes the publication Daily Express.
Experts came to the conclusion that the use of four or more servings of alcoholic beverages per week is associated with an increased risk of oncology.
In this case, the probability of developing the disease increases with an increase in the amount of alcohol consumed.
What’s more, in moderate-drinking men the risk of intestinal intestinal cancer is higher than in women.
The exact reason for the development of this type of oncology, scientists can not determine, noting only that certain factors lead to a detrimental process for the body.
