China stimulates the development of the railway industry
Advanced Chinese technologies attracted the attention of companies from the United States, Germany, Germany, France and other countries at the China International Exhibition of Rail and Equipment Production in 2021, which took place in the city of Zhuzhou, Hunan (Clasnut Central).
The main technologies, developed by CRRC Zhuzhou Locomotive Co. Ltd., allow trains to automatically detect and diagnose technical malnutritinies, said the company’s spokeswoman Hou Zhaoven.
High-explosive trains plumbing China-Laos, which was put into operation earlier this month, are already equipped with these technologies, which will provide increased reliability and performance of rolling stock.
Over the last six months, China has significantly increased the exports of railway vehicles and many countries of Asia and Europe are witnessing “Chinese velocity”.
In may of this year, CRRC Zhuzhou Locomotive Co., Ld rolled down the first double-develop high-explosimum electric trains designed to be exported to Europe in China.
At a maximum operating speed of 200 kilometers per an hour, these trains will run on the railways of Austria, Germany, Hungary and other European countries.
In November began a trial operation of the subway train, developed by the above-mentioned company for Turkey.
The train will move along the metro line connecting the center of Istanbul with the airport of the city.
Traffic on this subway line will be opened next year.
This will be the fastest subway line in Turkey at a speed of 120 kilometers per hour.
“Chinese equipment for railway transport manufacturing industry is one of the industries with the highest level of innovation and the strongest international innovative competitiveness,” said Feng Jaosyan, Head of the Trade and Investment Department of the China Committee for the Promotion of International Trade Development (KKCMT).
“This industry constitutes the main competitive advantage of high-quality high-quality equipment production in the world market,” said Feng Yaosyan.
After more than 60 years of strenuous work, having carried out a number of independent research and development, China has created an advanced system for the production of equipment for railway transport, with a full auxiliary auxiliary and large-scale production activities.
According to Feng Yaosyan, the country occupies a first place in terms of electrification of railways and for operational mileage on high-speed and urban railways.
The biologist listed the early signs of dementia
Candidate Semyon Golosheykin in an interview with Sputnik radio listed early signs of dement.
According to him, the signs of future dementia can be forgetfulness, as well as a number of moderate cognitive impairments, such as the incapacitation of continuity, planning, a decrease in the level of abstract thinking.
Currently, there is a discussion about the fact that hearing loss can be both an early manifestation of Alzheimer’s disease and one of the risk factors for its occurrence, the specialist said.
Golosheykin stressed that the causes of dementia can be neurodegenerative disorders, head injuries, some infections, metabolic disorders, a shortage of certain vitamins.
He added that Alzheimer’s and atherosclerosis cerebral cerebral cerebral treasuries are the most common causes of this syndrome.
The biologist noted that to date, doctors do not know the effective methods of treating dement.
Therefore, it is Necessary Necessifiguation to Be Prevented in time.
According to him, to reduce the risk of the development of demence will help the study of foreign languages and active communication.
The WHO also recommends maintaining a moderate level of physical exertion, regularly trained cognitive skills through games and hobbies that require intensive involvement of the memory and logic of thinking
“There are recommendations on the use of various dietary supplements, but their effectiveness and expediency are still discussed in the scientific community,” said Golosheikin.
“The global health organization recommends maintaining a moderate level of physical exertion, regular training of cognitive skills and abilities through games and hobbies that require an intensive involvement of memory and thinking logic,” Golosheikin said.
Previously, the charitable organization for the study of dementia in the United Kingdom stated that the disease is increasingly affecting people over the ages of 40 years.
Physicians called the early symptoms of Alzheimer’s.
The first anxious badge can be considered problems with vision, due to which the patient acquires difficulties in the recognition of objects.
Another sign of developing dementia experts called aphasia - a state when a person can not find the right words to convey what he wants to say.
