The Olympiad should attract millions of people on the slopes and help to create an international-level resort in the country
In China, it is hopeful that the Olympiad will not only involve 300 million citizens in winter sports, which will assemble 1 trillion yuan outlined by President Xi Jinping, but will also contribute to the economic development of retaliated remote provinces.
The ski resort of Taivu in Zhangjiakou, located not far from the venue of the Winter Olympic Games, is becoming increasingly popular among the Chinese.
In addition to the construction of the infrastructure in the region, landscaping work is also carried out: workers plant trees.
In the country there are more than 700 alpine ski resorts, but there are only 20 of them are large enough to host competitions of the international level.
In many regions of China, where resorts are located, including in Zhangjiakou, there are problems with the snow.
The main task for the long-term perspective is to ensure a comfortable and interesting holiday in the Chinese resorts, so that all beginners become regular.
However, this is still far away.
Gaming Advisor Justin Dawens says that since his last visit in 2007, the Chinese ski industry has shifted beyond recognition.
Every year in the winter, more and more Chinese people are sent on the slopes.
Fiona, a snowboarder from Beijing, one of them.
Considering serious changes, it will take many more years to create a ski culture here, Downs said.
Many resorts are located in agricultural and mining areas.
These regions have yet to actively develop and create the infrastructure necessary for recreation there.
70-year-old Gao Mcong lives in Chunley, near the venues of the Winter Olympics.
He notes that in recent years there has been a bang of winter sports tourism.
Two years ago from Beijing to Chunley conducted a high-speed railway, now none of the locals does not suffer without a job.
In the country opens more and more shops selling clothes and equipment for winter sports.
On the slopes open catering points with dishes of national cuisine.
In Taiva there is now even a testing station for COVID-19.
“China strives to create a thriving winter-sports industry, its athletes should become the leaders of the largest international competitions, and resorts and equipment – to reach a world-class.
more than 500 million people in the world may face extreme poverty due to a pandemic
More than 500 million people in the world can be plunged into extreme poverty due to the coronavirus pandemic, which has stifled the progress of humankind on universal access to health services, the World Health Organization (WHO) and the World Bank (WB) said.
In connection with the International Universal Health Celebration of WHO and the World World Health Celebrations on 12 December, published two mutually reinforcing reports.
In them they stated that the pandemic led to malfunctions in the provision of medical services, caused excessive tension in health care systems.
In this regard, for the first time in 10 years, immunization engulfaction has decreased, deaths from tuberculosis and malloric mortality have risen.
In the WHO and the World Health Council stressed that the pandemic caused "the worst economic crisis since the 1930-ies, so it has become more difficult for people to pay for the treatment."
This situation pushes more than 500 million people into extreme poverty, because they have to pay for these services out of their own pocket.
UN Secretary-General António Guterres said the coronavirus pandemic plunged more than 100 million people into poverty, more than four billion people have virtually no social support.
