Reuters: the Taiwanese Minister was disconnected from the broadcast on the “Summit for Democrat” at the request of the White house
Speech of the Minister of Digital Technologies of Tayyna Audrey Tang at a panel discussion during the US-organized “Sammita for Democracy” has been translated into mode without a video, according to the recording of the summit on YouTube.
Reuters with reference to the sources claims that the picture was disconnected at the request of the White house.
According to them, the reason was the map, on which Taiwan was allocated a separate color from the PRC, which considers the island its own territory.
The map, presented by Ms. Tang, was compiled by the South African non-governmental organization CIVIC and ranked world countries in terms of civil rights.
Taivania was singled out on it green as "free", and China, the DPRK, Laos, and Viet Nam - like "closed" as "closed".
After the Minister showed the map, the picture on its part was replaced by a screenshot with a note that the opinions of the participants of the discussion “do not necessarily express the position of the US government”.
PRC was not invited to “Summit for Democracy”.
Sources of Reuters note that the map, which was demonstrated by the Taiwanese minister, could go in continuity with the “one-China”, which is adhered to by Washington.
One of the sources of the agency said that after detaching the map, the U.S. National Security Advisor angerfully contacted the State Department, accusing him of revealing Taywan a separate country.
“Summit for Democrat” organized by Washington took place from December 9 to December 10 with the participation of representatives of 110 countries and territories, as well as civil associations and charities.
Russia was not invited for the summit.
During the “zero day” of the summit, the winner of the Nobel Peace Prize, the editor-in-chief of “Novaya Gazeta” Dmitry Muratov urged to create an international fund through which the money extracted through corrosion was donated for charity.
Earlier today, the Deputy Secretary of the Security Council of the Russian Federation Yury Averyanov said that the summit carried an “anti-Russian and anti-Chinese charge”.
