New Shepard spacecraft with six tourists on board made a sub-orbital flight
The New Shepard spaceship company Blue Origin with six tourists on board made a suborbital flight on Saturday, December 11.
The voyage, broadcast on the company's website, lasted for a total of more than ten minutes, after which the capsule with the passengers descended to the Ground, according to TASS.
The launch of the carrier rocket was carried out from the cosmodrome in the area of the American city of Van Horn (Texas).
The ship rose to a height of a little more than 100 km, space tourists were in a state of weightlessness.
The launch vehicle itself normally landed at the site of the cosmodrome.
On July 20, Blue Origin successfully carried out the first sub-orbital flight of the New Shepard spacecraft with passengers on board.
