“China strengthens COVID-19 prevention and control of COVID-19 in cities where land checkpoints
The joint mechanism for the prevention and control of the State Council of the People's Republic of China has issued a circular to strengthen the prevention and control of the COVID-19 epidemic in cities where land checkpoints are located, in order to further prevent the import of infection from abroad.
According to the Circular, people who leave these cities must provide a negative COVID-19 nucleic nucleuric acid test obtained within 48 hours before departure.
Those who come to the cities in which land checkpoints are located must take at least one nucleic acid COVID-19 test upon arrival.
The document says that these requirements will be in effect from the day when the relevant administrative units of the provincial level will determine and publish the zones of these cities, until March 15, 2022.
In addition, it is noted that the cities in which land checkpoints are located and which meet certain conditions can consider the possibility of creating buffer zones for the prevention and control of the COVID-19 epidemic within their jurisdiction.
