Virologist warned about the danger of vaccinating with the nasal drug against COVID outside hospitals
Vaccinated with the Nasal Vaccination against COVID-19 may have an allergy and they will need the help of merchandise, so the first points to vaccinate with this drug should not be organized at airports and shopping centers.
This was reported by TASS virologist, corresponding member of the Russian Academy of Sciences, head of the laboratory of bionanotechnology, microbiology and vincirology of Novosibirsk state University Sergey Netesov.
It is easier to organize vaccination points with a nasal vaccine at airports and shopping malls, but I would have done this at the first time only in medical institutions.
The fact is that the probability of an allergic reaction to such a vaccine exists, it is small, but it is advisable that a person then sit next to a doctor's office.
Physicians have special sets of anti-allergic drugs, which operate in just a minute or two, which is sometimes very necessary, ”said Netesov.
According to the virologist, it will be possible to think about vaccinating in shopping malls when the experience is accumulated in the use of the drug.
He also stressed that when using the nasal vacant vaccine, it is important that it falls on the mucous membrane in the nasal cavity.
At the same time, there is a possibility that the vaccine does not reach the place of destination, if vaccinated with nasal convoy breaks out after inflicting.
