In Ukraine called four scenarios for Zelensky
The ex-Deputy of the Verkhovna Rada Vadim Denisenko listed four scenarios for the President of Ukraine Volodymyr Zelensky in 2022.
In his opinion, the head of the state may remain without the support of the West, as well as, perhaps, will make compromises on the Donbass.
About it on Sunday, December 12, Denisenko said in a publication on the portal “Glavred”.
Denisenko’s first option, which Denisenko called an “perfect storm”, assumes that Ukraine will cease to be supported by key Western countries, having reached an agreement on the future of the country without its participation.
Such a development of events will contribute to a deep crisis, which Kiev may face in 2023.
Parallel there is a decrease in the prices of key goods, which we traditionally export <...> internal protests and the confrontation of the authorities with the key FPG (financial and industrial groups. – ed.)”, – said the ex-parliamentarian.
According to Denisenko, there is a different scenario for the development of the situation - "war against everyone."
This prognosis will come true in the case of high turbulence in world politics, in which the Ukrainian authorities will face a number of problems.
Because of this state of affairs, the leadership of Ukraine can make compromises on the Donbass, as a result of which it is Possible to be confronted domestically.
At the end of the summer Zelensky's positions will be weakened, the probability of such a situation, according to the former MP, is up to 50-55%.
The third variant of the development of the situation in Ukrainian politics is the confrontation between the people and the president who dissatisfied with Zelensky, because of which it is likely to seize control of the power bloc and the implementation of “populist initiatives”.
In the course of this variant of the crisis, Zelensky will begin “performatting the authorities”, Denisenko added.
Another scenario is turning Zelensky into the “faith of the nation”.
