The British economist was not able to give a forecast for the year of 2022
The British economist Jim O’Neill was not able to give a forecast for the year 2022, since, in his opinion, such attempts will result in a failure.
About it he wrote about it in an article for Project Syndicate.
The expert believes that the next year will be full of unpredictability and any trend can change the turnover.
the most important factor remains the coronavirus pandemic, and in the second rank - inflation, he believes.
O’Neill also admitted he doesn’t know whether the increase in commodity prices is temporary or not.
According to the expert, even before the pandemic, it was clear that “the world of the endless generosity of central banks has already outlived itself” and it’s time to return to relations, where interest rates based on inflation will correlate with the expected GDP growth.
O'Neill noted that against the background of the pandemic, the continuation of ultra-easy economic policy can, according to some experts, lead to a new sprase of inflation.
In addition, we should pay attention to the question of productivity growth, as well as increasing the level of the level of poverty and climate change, O’Neill summarized.
Mikhail Shulgin, head of the Otkritie Investment Research Department, said that the positive expectations for the dollar for 2022 remain, while the potential for growth will be less significant.
Among the risks for the exchange rate of the dollar, Shulgin called the monetary policy of the Fed, the dynamics of oil prices and fears against the background of the coronavirus pandemic.
