The Russians gave the car dealers about 4.5% of the country's country's GDP
According to the results of 10 months of in 2021, the Russians spent on the purchase of new cars 2 trillion 784 billion rubles, which is 28% more than in the same period of last year, according to statistical data, according to statistical data of the Agency Russian Automotive Market Research (NAPI).
To understand the scoring - about the same amount (about 3 trillion rubles) was expended by the state to support the citizens and the economy during the coronavirus pandemic.
In last September at a meeting of the leaders of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization, President Vladimir Putin said that such an amount is comparable to more than 4.5% of the country's gross domestic (GVP) for 2020.
In terms of revenues in the Russian market, the Korean brand Kia leads.
For 10 months of this year, he was able to sell cars in the amount of 325.7 billion rubles, which is almost 24% more than a year earlier.
The Kia-complicated Hyundai brand has an increase even more significant - more than 35%, and the proceed from the sale of cars is estimated at 279.3 billion rubles.
In the leading positions of this brand to an increase in the weighted average price of the car - for a year it grew by almost 21%, to 1.94 million rubles - only Changan, Chery, Geely and Mercedes-Benz were stronger.
At the same time, the volume of sales of Korean brands did not increase so much: according to the statistics of the committee of automotive Manufacturers of the Association of European Businesses in Russia, in quantitative terms, Kia sold 9.4% more cars over the same period than a year earlier.
Hyundai - by almost 12 percent.
Closes the top three leaders in terms of sales in monetary terms, the Japanese Toyota - the Russians spent 275.5 billion roubles for 10 months, which is 14% more than a year earlier than a year before.
Behind the Japanese followed by Mercedes-Benz with an indicator of 266.1 billion rubles (+ 75%) - the German premium brand has also increased the volume of sales (by 37%), and the weighted-double-dense price of the car (almost 28%, to 8.2 million rubles).
“The Mercedes-Benz at the same time there is a good increase in sales and a weighted average price - more, for example, than BMW - hence a greater increase in financial capacity, - the general director of NAPI Tatiana Arabadji explained.
According to the growth of sales, fantastic indicators are demonstrated by Chinese brands, which have also significantly increased the financial capacity this year.”
The Russian Lada in terms of the dynamics of income growth demonstrates the average market indicators (plus 28%), on the cars of this brand the Russians spent 229.4 billion ruproble for 10 months.
At the level of last year in terms of financial capacity are the companies, sales of cars of which in pieces in 2021 fell: in particular, Volkswagen, Mitsubishi and Nissan.
UAZ and at all in minus - for 10 months the Russians spent on SUSUV and pickers of this brand 12 billion rubles against 12.4 billion rubles a year earlier.
Against the background of problems with the supply of automotive components and interruptions in the production, which engulfed the entire global automotive industry, car companies continue to continuously adjust prices - the same AvtoVAZ increased the cost of Lada models seven times in a year, the last rise in price (8-10 thousand rubles) occurred at the end of November.
Rewrite price tags for their products and other automakers regularly.
The volumes of the automotive market of Russia in monetary terms will further increase - in addition to the shortage of cars, inflation is made to this, as well as the desire of automakers to retrieve past losses, according to experts.
In conditions of a shortage of cars, I think that many automakers were even able to partially shift the costs to the consumer of past periods, which they could not lay in the price of cars earlier.
says VTB Occupation analyst Vladimir Bespalov.
I believe that in financial terms, car manufacturers feel very good now, maintaining a high margin of sales.”
An invisible indicator of this is the growth rate of the cost of cars, which is observed during 2021, the prices of new cars are growing faster than inflation, the expert clarifies.
In the long term, the market will grow in numerical terms, and in monetary, but mainly due to inflation and complicating the design of the machines themselves, Bespalov predicts.
With an increase in the supply of opportunities to raise prices will be limited.
In monetary terms, the Russian car market will continue to grow next year, even if an increase in the cost of cars slows, car manufacturers will be able to receive their income at the expense of volumes, notes the independent consultant for the automotive industry Sergey Burgazliyev.
Taking into account the increased demand and insufficient supply, now automakers are striving to get the largest profit from each car sold, Burgazliyev notes.
An increase in the volume of production of cars is not expected at least in the next six months, while in Russia the stimulus is heated by the insecure of citizens in the future.
Against the backdrop of the current situation on the market, cars turned out to be a good object for an investment - a car bought a year ago, even with a mile, now you can sell more velocious than the original cost, the expert says.
Biden spoke about the relocation of the U.S. military to Ukraine in the event of a Russian invasion
The leadership of the United States has never considered the sending of the American military to Ukraine in the event of an “invasion” of Russia.
Such a statement was made by U.S. President Joe Biden.
“There has never been such plans,” said the head of the White house, answering the journalist’s question about whether the U.S. abandoned such an idea.
Biden noted that in the event of an escalation of the situation around Ukraine, Russia will face economic consequences.
At the same time, he stressed that the United States and NATO do not have an obligation to use military force to protect Ukraine in the event of an escalation.
The American leader also said that the possibility of the use of American troops unilaterally for the defense of Ukraine does not stand on the agenda.
Biden explained that if Russia invades the territory of Ukraine, the United States will transfer forces to Eastern European NATO countries (Bulgaria, Hungary, Latvia, Lithuania, Poland, Romania, the Czech Republic and Estonia).
“We will have to send more American and NATO troops to the eastern flank, B9 – all those non-NATO countries against which we have a sacred obligation to protect them from any Russian attack,” Biden said.
Earlier, the press Secretary of the President of Russia Dmitry Pesskov stressed that Moscow does not have its intention to invade the territory of Ukraine.
At the same time, he pointed out that Moscow sees a problem in the combat use of drones supplied by Turkey by Kiev, as well as in the fact that "American weapons are approaching our territory."
