Alexander Sokurov’s film received the European Oscar for the best montage
Denominated for "Oscar" Russian film "Unclear fists" was awarded the European Film academia (it is also called "Europe "Oscar") in the nomination "Best editing", reports "Moskovsky Komsomolets".
The jury of the competition, who voted online due to the difficult epidemiological situation, appreciated the outstanding skill of the filmmakers.
Yasmila Zhbánnich (Bosnia) "Where are you going, Aida?"
The main character of the ribbon - an interpreter at the UN mission, who is trying to save her family during the war in Yugoslavia.
As for the drama "Squeeping fists", shot by Kira Kovalenko (a graduate of Alexander Sokurov's workshop), then this film tells about the complex relationship of the domineering father and those who want to get free from paternal tutelage of growing children in North Ossetia.
Earlier it was announced that this film was nominated for an Oscar as the best film shot in a foreign language.
